# Summary
The most relevant implementation for an agent with longterm memory is in `camel/memories/agent_memories.py` where `LongtermAgentMemory` combines chat history and vector DB memory. Example usage patterns for memory-enabled agents are in `examples/memories/agent_memory_example.py` (chat history memory) and `examples/memories/agent_memory_vector_db_example.py` (vector DB memory). The `MemoryToolkit` in `camel/toolkits/memory_toolkit.py` provides tools for human interaction with memory (save/load/clear). The test file `test/memories/test_agent_memories.py` validates the memory implementations.

These files together provide the components, usage examples, and testing needed to create an agent with longterm memory and human interaction tools. You can base your script on these examples and use `LongtermAgentMemory` for the memory implementation.
